 at 02:15, appending output to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log. The script file was found corrupted (leftover heredoc text) and was rewritten to a working POSIX sh script, made executable, and functionally verified. Performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured baseline boot_id and cron/log health, issued a self-acknowledging systemctl reboot, polled until the node returned, proved the boot_id changed, and confirmed cron service, crontab entry, script, and log file all survived and continued to function post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance and found it corrupted with leftover heredoc/shell text\",\"Rewrote the script to a correct POSIX sh script and set ownership root:root, mode 0755\",\"Ran the script manually to confirm it produces expected output\",\"Added a root crontab entry: 15 2 * * * /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance >> /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log 2>&1\",\"Manually ran the exact crontab command line to confirm it appends correctly to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log\",\"Confirmed cron.service is enabled and active on node1\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and health (cron active, crontab present, log content) before restart\",\"Issued a backgrounded systemctl reboot on node1 so the acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again, observing connection reset/timeout during the restart window\",\"Verified boot_id changed after restart, proving an actual reboot occurred\",\"Re-verified cron active/enabled, crontab entry intact, script intact and executable, and prior log entry preserved post-restart\",\"Re-ran the maintenance command post-restart to confirm continued correct append behavior\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Script /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance exists, correct, and executable\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1f1c9d2413fe444d\",\"cmd-39fbb46f6f49416e\",\"cmd-ba5384af15dd46cc\"],\"summary\":\"Found script corrupted, rewrote it to a valid POSIX sh script with 0755 perms, and confirmed it runs and prints the expected inventory line.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cron job scheduled for 02:15 daily writing to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c6a0738725d44512\",\"cmd-de188a9bfba341ab\"],\"summary\":\"Installed root crontab entry '15 2 * * * /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance >> /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log 2>&1' and manually executed the exact command line, confirming output is correctly appended to the log file.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cron daemon active/enabled so schedule will actually fire\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f3d4328fc48c4ba0\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl showed cron.service enabled and active (running) on node1.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-498d886ee2114c22\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id, uptime, cron active status, crontab contents, and log contents prior to restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement returns before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2038c318ae58433f\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sleep 1 && systemctl reboot' returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately, then subsequent execs failed with connection reset/timeout confirming the node went down.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 boot identity changed after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-791c83af6e8e415b\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart boot_id (011daef2-2b82-41e2-bc08-230e5d870eea) differs from baseline boot_id (cfdbaef8-7705-46ed-b0cd-c985235704ea), proving an actual kernel restart occurred.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 required services and data recovered after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7ed662f92472464b\",\"cmd-662e885c75da462d\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, cron.service is active/enabled, the crontab entry and script remain intact/executable, the prior log entry persisted, and re-running the job appended a new line successfully.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1's root crontab to run /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance daily at 02:15, appending output to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log. The script file was found corrupted (leftover heredoc text) and was rewritten to a working POSIX sh script, made executable, and functionally verified. Performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured baseline boot_id and cron/log health, issued a self-acknowledging systemctl reboot, polled until the node returned, proved the boot_id changed, and confirmed cron service, crontab entry, script, and log file all survived and continued to function post-restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance and found it corrupted with leftover heredoc/shell text","Rewrote the script to a correct POSIX sh script and set ownership root:root, mode 0755","Ran the script manually to confirm it produces expected output","Added a root crontab entry: 15 2 * * * /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance >> /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log 2>&1","Manually ran the exact crontab command line to confirm it appends correctly to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log","Confirmed cron.service is enabled and active on node1","Captured baseline boot_id and health (cron active, crontab present, log content) before restart","Issued a backgrounded systemctl reboot on node1 so the acknowledgement returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again, observing connection reset/timeout during the restart window","Verified boot_id changed after restart, proving an actual reboot occurred","Re-verified cron active/enabled, crontab entry intact, script intact and executable, and prior log entry preserved post-restart","Re-ran the maintenance command post-restart to confirm continued correct append behavior"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Script /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance exists, correct, and executable","command_ids":["cmd-1f1c9d2413fe444d","cmd-39fbb46f6f49416e","cmd-ba5384af15dd46cc"],"summary":"Found script corrupted, rewrote it to a valid POSIX sh script with 0755 perms, and confirmed it runs and prints the expected inventory line."},{"requirement":"Cron job scheduled for 02:15 daily writing to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log","command_ids":["cmd-c6a0738725d44512","cmd-de188a9bfba341ab"],"summary":"Installed root crontab entry '15 2 * * * /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance >> /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log 2>&1' and manually executed the exact command line, confirming output is correctly appended to the log file."},{"requirement":"Cron daemon active/enabled so schedule will actually fire","command_ids":["cmd-f3d4328fc48c4ba0"],"summary":"systemctl showed cron.service enabled and active (running) on node1."},{"requirement":"node1 healthy baseline before restart","command_ids":["cmd-498d886ee2114c22"],"summary":"Captured boot_id, uptime, cron active status, crontab contents, and log contents prior to restart."},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement returns before disconnection","command_ids":["cmd-2038c318ae58433f"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'sleep 1 && systemctl reboot' returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately, then subsequent execs failed with connection reset/timeout confirming the node went down."},{"requirement":"node1 boot identity changed after restart","command_ids":["cmd-791c83af6e8e415b"],"summary":"Post-restart boot_id (011daef2-2b82-41e2-bc08-230e5d870eea) differs from baseline boot_id (cfdbaef8-7705-46ed-b0cd-c985235704ea), proving an actual kernel restart occurred."},{"requirement":"node1 required services and data recovered after restart","command_ids":["cmd-7ed662f92472464b","cmd-662e885c75da462d"],"summary":"After restart, cron.service is active/enabled, the crontab entry and script remain intact/executable, the prior log entry persisted, and re-running the job appended a new line successfully."}]},"ttft_ms":1349,"type":"result","duration_ms":75684,"uuid":"4c5bb51c-b927-415c-bda3-de748ebd5af8","ttft_stream_ms":793,"time_to_request_ms":44,"queued_turn_count":0}
